IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cbca-core-definitions`
IMPORT `cb1-nouns`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Part IV, sections 19 to 23 (the registered
-- office, the corporate records, access to them, their form, the corporate seal). The register of
-- individuals with significant control (sections 21.1 to 21.4) is in cb1-part4-isc-register.l4.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Justice Canada consolidation current to
-- 2026-09-30, which is not an official version; nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RULE. Each rule is named `<what it decides> within s <section>`. A rule that says a duty
-- has been met takes the facts that the duty turns on and returns TRUE when it has been met. An offence
-- is two rules: whether the person is guilty, and the most a court may impose.

§ `Part IV -- Registered office and records`

§§ `s 19 registered office`

-- src:242 | 19 (1) A corporation shall at all times have a registered office in the province in Canada specified in its articles.
@ref CBCA s 19(1) registered office (src:242)
GIVEN `the corporation has a registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registered office is in the province in Canada specified in the articles` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation has the registered office that s 19(1) requires` MEANS
        `the corporation has a registered office`
    AND `the registered office is in the province in Canada specified in the articles`

-- s 19(2): the notice goes "together with any articles that designate or change the province where the
-- registered office of the corporation is located". A notice is a thing that was sent or was not.
-- src:244 | (2) A notice of registered office in the form that the Director fixes shall be sent to the Director together with any articles that designate or change the province where the registered office of the corporation is located.
@ref CBCA s 19(2) notice of registered office (src:244)
GIVEN `the articles designate or change the province where the registered office is located` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a notice of registered office in the form that the Director fixes was sent to the Director together with the articles` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation has complied with the duty to send a notice of registered office within s 19(2)` MEANS
        (NOT `the articles designate or change the province where the registered office is located`)
    OR  `a notice of registered office in the form that the Director fixes was sent to the Director together with the articles`

-- src:246 | (3) The directors of a corporation may change the place and address of the registered office within the province specified in the articles.
@ref CBCA s 19(3) change of address (src:246)
GIVEN `the new place and address are within the province specified in the articles` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the directors may change the place and address of the registered office within s 19(3)` MEANS
    `the new place and address are within the province specified in the articles`

-- src:248 | (4) A corporation shall send to the Director, within fifteen days of any change of address of its registered office, a notice in the form that the Director fixes and the Director shall file it.
@ref CBCA s 19(4) notice of change of address (src:248)
DECIDE `the fifteen-day limit of s 19(4)` IS `Time limit` WITH
    `number of units` IS 15
    `unit of time` IS `calendar days`

-- src:248 | (4) A corporation shall send to the Director, within fifteen days of any change of address of its registered office, a notice in the form that the Director fixes and the Director shall file it.
@ref CBCA s 19(4) notice of change of address (src:248)
GIVEN `the day the address of the registered office changed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to send the notice of change of address within s 19(4)` MEANS
    `the last day of` `the fifteen-day limit of s 19(4)` `counted from` `the day the address of the registered office changed`

-- src:248 | (4) A corporation shall send to the Director, within fifteen days of any change of address of its registered office, a notice in the form that the Director fixes and the Director shall file it.
@ref CBCA s 19(4) notice of change of address (src:248)
GIVEN `the day the address of the registered office changed` IS A DATE
      `the day the notice was sent to the Director` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the notice of change of address was sent in time within s 19(4)` MEANS
    `done within the time limit` `the fifteen-day limit of s 19(4)` `the day the address of the registered office changed` `the day the notice was sent to the Director`

-- src:248 | (4) A corporation shall send to the Director, within fifteen days of any change of address of its registered office, a notice in the form that the Director fixes and the Director shall file it.
@ref CBCA s 19(4) notice of change of address (src:248)
GIVEN `a notice of change of address in the form that the Director fixes was sent to the Director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director must file the notice of change of address within s 19(4)` MEANS
    `a notice of change of address in the form that the Director fixes was sent to the Director`

§§ `s 20 corporate records`

-- The four kinds of record s 20(1) lists. A field is TRUE when the corporation prepares and maintains
-- that kind of record.
-- src:250 | 20 (1) A corporation shall prepare and maintain, at its registered office or at any other place in Canada designated by the directors, records containing
-- src:251 | (a) the articles and the by-laws, and all amendments thereto, and a copy of any unanimous shareholder agreement;
-- src:252 | (b) minutes of meetings and resolutions of shareholders;
-- src:253 | (c) copies of all notices required by section 106 or 113; and
-- src:254 | (d) a securities register that complies with section 50.
@ref CBCA s 20(1) corporate records (src:250-254)
DECLARE `Corporate records kept under s 20(1)` HAS
    `the articles and the by-laws, and all amendments thereto, and a copy of any unanimous shareholder agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `minutes of meetings and resolutions of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
    `copies of all notices required by section 106 or 113` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: sections 106 and 113 (piece cb2)
    `a securities register that complies with section 50` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: section 50 (piece cb2)

-- src:250 | 20 (1) A corporation shall prepare and maintain, at its registered office or at any other place in Canada designated by the directors, records containing
-- src:251 | (a) the articles and the by-laws, and all amendments thereto, and a copy of any unanimous shareholder agreement;
-- src:252 | (b) minutes of meetings and resolutions of shareholders;
-- src:253 | (c) copies of all notices required by section 106 or 113; and
-- src:254 | (d) a securities register that complies with section 50.
@ref CBCA s 20(1) corporate records (src:250-254)
GIVEN records IS A `Corporate records kept under s 20(1)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation keeps all the records s 20(1) lists` MEANS
        records's `the articles and the by-laws, and all amendments thereto, and a copy of any unanimous shareholder agreement`
    AND records's `minutes of meetings and resolutions of shareholders`
    AND records's `copies of all notices required by section 106 or 113`
    AND records's `a securities register that complies with section 50`

-- src:256 | (2) In addition to the records described in subsection (1), a corporation shall prepare and maintain adequate accounting records and records containing minutes of meetings and resolutions of the directors and any committee thereof.
@ref CBCA s 20(2) directors records (src:256)
DECLARE `Directors and accounting records kept under s 20(2)` HAS
    `adequate accounting records` IS A BOOLEAN
    `records containing minutes of meetings and resolutions of the directors and any committee of the directors` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:256 | (2) In addition to the records described in subsection (1), a corporation shall prepare and maintain adequate accounting records and records containing minutes of meetings and resolutions of the directors and any committee thereof.
@ref CBCA s 20(2) directors records (src:256)
GIVEN records IS A `Directors and accounting records kept under s 20(2)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation keeps all the records s 20(2) lists` MEANS
        records's `adequate accounting records`
    AND records's `records containing minutes of meetings and resolutions of the directors and any committee of the directors`

-- s 20(2.1): six years after the end of the financial year; "subject to" another Act that provides for a
-- longer period, in which case that longer period is the one that counts.
-- src:258 | (2.1) Subject to any other Act of Parliament and to any Act of the legislature of a province that provides for a longer retention period, a corporation shall retain the accounting records referred to in subsection (2) for a period of six years after the end of the financial year to which the records relate.
@ref CBCA s 20(2.1) retention of accounting records (src:258)
DECIDE `the six-year retention period of s 20(2.1)` IS `Time limit` WITH
    `number of units` IS 6
    `unit of time` IS `calendar years`

-- src:258 | (2.1) Subject to any other Act of Parliament and to any Act of the legislature of a province that provides for a longer retention period, a corporation shall retain the accounting records referred to in subsection (2) for a period of six years after the end of the financial year to which the records relate.
@ref CBCA s 20(2.1) retention of accounting records (src:258)
GIVEN `the last day of the financial year to which the accounting records relate` IS A DATE
      `the longer retention period that another Act of Parliament or a provincial Act provides, if there is one` IS A MAYBE `Time limit`   -- out of range: other Acts of Parliament and provincial Acts (outside the Act)
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day the corporation must retain the accounting records within s 20(2.1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the longer retention period that another Act of Parliament or a provincial Act provides, if there is one`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the end of the six years`
    WHEN JUST longer THEN
        IF `the last day of` longer `counted from` `the last day of the financial year to which the accounting records relate` AT LEAST `the end of the six years`
        THEN `the last day of` longer `counted from` `the last day of the financial year to which the accounting records relate`
        ELSE `the end of the six years`
    WHERE
        `the end of the six years` MEANS `the last day of` `the six-year retention period of s 20(2.1)` `counted from` `the last day of the financial year to which the accounting records relate`

-- s 20(3): where a body corporate is continued, "records" in paragraph (1)(b) and subsection (2) includes
-- similar records the law required it to maintain before it was continued.
-- src:260 | (3) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(b) and subsection (2), where a body corporate is continued under this Act, “records” includes similar records required by law to be maintained by the body corporate before it was so continued.
@ref CBCA s 20(3) records of continued corporations (src:260)
GIVEN `the record is one described in paragraph 20(1)(b) or subsection 20(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body corporate was continued under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the record is similar to those and was required by law to be maintained by the body corporate before it was continued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the record counts as a record for paragraph 20(1)(b) and subsection 20(2) within s 20(3)` MEANS
        `the record is one described in paragraph 20(1)(b) or subsection 20(2)`
    OR  (    `the body corporate was continued under this Act`
         AND `the record is similar to those and was required by law to be maintained by the body corporate before it was continued`)

-- s 20(4): the directors' records and accounting records are kept at the registered office or "at such
-- other place as the directors think fit", and are open to inspection by the directors at all reasonable
-- times. The place need not be in Canada, so the rule does not use the Part IV place enumeration.
-- src:262 | (4) The records described in subsection (2) shall be kept at the registered office of the corporation or at such other place as the directors think fit and shall at all reasonable times be open to inspection by the directors.
@ref CBCA s 20(4) place of directors records (src:262)
GIVEN `the records are kept at the registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors think fit the place where the records are kept` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the records are open to inspection by the directors at all reasonable times` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the records of subsection 20(2) are kept as s 20(4) requires` MEANS
        (`the records are kept at the registered office` OR `the directors think fit the place where the records are kept`)
    AND `the records are open to inspection by the directors at all reasonable times`

-- s 20(5.1): "Despite subsections (1) and (5), but subject to the Income Tax Act, the Excise Tax Act, the
-- Customs Act and any other Act administered by the Minister of National Revenue", records may be kept
-- outside Canada if (a) they are available for inspection by computer terminal or other technology
-- during regular office hours at the registered office or another place in Canada designated by the
-- directors and (b) the corporation provides the technical assistance.
-- src:266 | (5.1) Despite subsections (1) and (5), but subject to the Income Tax Act, the Excise Tax Act, the Customs Act and any other Act administered by the Minister of National Revenue, a corporation may keep all or any of its corporate records and accounting records referred to in subsection (1) or (2) at a place outside Canada, if
-- src:267 | (a) the records are available for inspection, by means of a computer terminal or other technology, during regular office hours at the registered office or any other place in Canada designated by the directors; and
-- src:268 | (b) the corporation provides the technical assistance to facilitate an inspection referred to in paragraph (a).
@ref CBCA s 20(5.1) when records or registers kept outside Canada (src:266-268)
GIVEN `an Act administered by the Minister of National Revenue requires the records to be kept in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: the Income Tax Act, the Excise Tax Act, the Customs Act and other Acts (outside the Act)
      `the records are available for inspection, by means of a computer terminal or other technology, during regular office hours at the registered office or any other place in Canada designated by the directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation provides the technical assistance to facilitate an inspection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may keep the records at a place outside Canada within s 20(5.1)` MEANS
        (NOT `an Act administered by the Minister of National Revenue requires the records to be kept in Canada`)
    AND `the records are available for inspection, by means of a computer terminal or other technology, during regular office hours at the registered office or any other place in Canada designated by the directors`
    AND `the corporation provides the technical assistance to facilitate an inspection`

-- src:250 | 20 (1) A corporation shall prepare and maintain, at its registered office or at any other place in Canada designated by the directors, records containing
-- src:264 | (5) If accounting records of a corporation are kept outside Canada, accounting records adequate to enable the directors to ascertain the financial position of the corporation with reasonable accuracy on a quarterly basis shall be kept at the registered office or any other place in Canada designated by the directors.
-- src:266 | (5.1) Despite subsections (1) and (5), but subject to the Income Tax Act, the Excise Tax Act, the Customs Act and any other Act administered by the Minister of National Revenue, a corporation may keep all or any of its corporate records and accounting records referred to in subsection (1) or (2) at a place outside Canada, if
@ref CBCA s 20(1), s 20(5), s 20(5.1) place of the corporate records (src:250 src:264 src:266)
GIVEN place IS A `Place where corporate records are kept (Part IV)`
      `the corporation may keep the records outside Canada under subsection 20(5.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporate records are kept at a permitted place within s 20(1) and s 20(5.1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `at the registered office of the corporation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `at another place in Canada designated by the directors` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `at a place in Canada that the directors have not designated` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `at a place outside Canada` THEN `the corporation may keep the records outside Canada under subsection 20(5.1)`

-- s 20(5): "If accounting records of a corporation are kept outside Canada, accounting records adequate to
-- enable the directors to ascertain the financial position of the corporation with reasonable accuracy on
-- a quarterly basis shall be kept at the registered office or any other place in Canada designated by the
-- directors." Subsection (5.1) applies "despite" it, so a corporation that may keep the records outside
-- Canada under (5.1) need not also keep a set in Canada.
-- src:264 | (5) If accounting records of a corporation are kept outside Canada, accounting records adequate to enable the directors to ascertain the financial position of the corporation with reasonable accuracy on a quarterly basis shall be kept at the registered office or any other place in Canada designated by the directors.
-- src:266 | (5.1) Despite subsections (1) and (5), but subject to the Income Tax Act, the Excise Tax Act, the Customs Act and any other Act administered by the Minister of National Revenue, a corporation may keep all or any of its corporate records and accounting records referred to in subsection (1) or (2) at a place outside Canada, if
@ref CBCA s 20(5), s 20(5.1) accounting records kept outside Canada (src:264 src:266)
GIVEN `the accounting records are kept outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation may keep the records outside Canada under subsection 20(5.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `accounting records adequate to ascertain the financial position of the corporation with reasonable accuracy on a quarterly basis are kept at the registered office or another place in Canada designated by the directors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation has complied with the duty to keep quarterly accounting records in Canada within s 20(5)` MEANS
        (NOT `the accounting records are kept outside Canada`)
    OR  `the corporation may keep the records outside Canada under subsection 20(5.1)`
    OR  `accounting records adequate to ascertain the financial position of the corporation with reasonable accuracy on a quarterly basis are kept at the registered office or another place in Canada designated by the directors`

-- s 20(6): an offence "without reasonable cause".
-- src:270 | (6) A corporation that, without reasonable cause, fails to comply with this section is guilty of an offence and liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars.
@ref CBCA s 20(6) offence (src:270)
GIVEN `the corporation fails to comply with section 20` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation is guilty of an offence within s 20(6)` MEANS
        `the corporation fails to comply with section 20`
    AND (NOT `the corporation has reasonable cause`)

-- src:270 | (6) A corporation that, without reasonable cause, fails to comply with this section is guilty of an offence and liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars.
@ref CBCA s 20(6) offence (src:270)
GIVETH A `Maximum punishment for an offence in Parts I to VI`
`the most a court may impose on summary conviction within s 20(6)` MEANS
    `Maximum punishment for an offence in Parts I to VI` WITH
        `maximum fine in dollars` IS 5000
        `maximum imprisonment in months` IS NOTHING

§§ `s 21 access to corporate records`

-- The persons s 21(1) names, in the text's order, and the rest of the world ("any other person").
-- src:272 | 21 (1) Subject to subsection (1.1), shareholders and creditors of a corporation, their personal representatives and the Director may examine the records described in subsection 20(1) during the usual business hours of the corporation, and may take extracts from the records, free of charge, and, if the corporation is a distributing corporation, any other person may do so on payment of a reasonable fee.
@ref CBCA s 21(1) access to corporate records (src:272)
DECLARE `Person seeking to examine the corporate records (s 21)` IS ONE OF
    `a shareholder of the corporation`
    `a creditor of the corporation`
    `a personal representative of a shareholder or creditor of the corporation`
    `the Director`
    `any other person`

-- src:272 | 21 (1) Subject to subsection (1.1), shareholders and creditors of a corporation, their personal representatives and the Director may examine the records described in subsection 20(1) during the usual business hours of the corporation, and may take extracts from the records, free of charge, and, if the corporation is a distributing corporation, any other person may do so on payment of a reasonable fee.
-- src:274 | (1.1) Any person described in subsection (1) who wishes to examine the securities register of a distributing corporation must first make a request to the corporation or its agent or mandatary, accompanied by an affidavit referred to in subsection (7). On receipt of the affidavit, the corporation or its agent or mandatary shall allow the applicant access to the securities register during the corporation’s usual business hours, and, on payment of a reasonable fee, provide the applicant with an extract from the securities register.
@ref CBCA s 21(1), s 21(1.1) access to corporate records (src:272 src:274)
DECLARE `Access to the corporate records under s 21(1) and s 21(1.1)` IS ONE OF
    `may examine the records during the usual business hours and take extracts, free of charge`
    `may examine the records during the usual business hours and take extracts, on payment of a reasonable fee`
    `may examine the securities register during the usual business hours once the affidavit is received, and have an extract on payment of a reasonable fee`
    `must first make a request to the corporation or its agent or mandatary, accompanied by an affidavit referred to in subsection 21(7)`
    `has no right of access under s 21(1)`

-- (1): shareholders, creditors, their personal representatives and the Director, free of charge; and, if the
-- corporation is a distributing corporation, any other person on payment of a reasonable fee.
-- (1.1): a person described in (1) who wishes to examine the securities register of a distributing
-- corporation must first send a request with an affidavit; the corporation then lets them examine it
-- and, on a reasonable fee, gives an extract.
-- src:272 | 21 (1) Subject to subsection (1.1), shareholders and creditors of a corporation, their personal representatives and the Director may examine the records described in subsection 20(1) during the usual business hours of the corporation, and may take extracts from the records, free of charge, and, if the corporation is a distributing corporation, any other person may do so on payment of a reasonable fee.
-- src:274 | (1.1) Any person described in subsection (1) who wishes to examine the securities register of a distributing corporation must first make a request to the corporation or its agent or mandatary, accompanied by an affidavit referred to in subsection (7). On receipt of the affidavit, the corporation or its agent or mandatary shall allow the applicant access to the securities register during the corporation’s usual business hours, and, on payment of a reasonable fee, provide the applicant with an extract from the securities register.
@ref CBCA s 21(1), s 21(1.1) access to corporate records (src:272 src:274)
GIVEN person IS A `Person seeking to examine the corporate records (s 21)`
      `the corporation is a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: section 2(1) (keel)
      `the person wishes to examine the securities register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has made a request accompanied by an affidavit referred to in subsection 21(7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Access to the corporate records under s 21(1) and s 21(1.1)`
`the access the person has to the corporate records within s 21(1) and s 21(1.1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the corporation is a distributing corporation` AND `the person wishes to examine the securities register`
            THEN IF `the person has made a request accompanied by an affidavit referred to in subsection 21(7)`
                 THEN `may examine the securities register during the usual business hours once the affidavit is received, and have an extract on payment of a reasonable fee`
                 ELSE `must first make a request to the corporation or its agent or mandatary, accompanied by an affidavit referred to in subsection 21(7)`
        IF person EQUALS `any other person`
            THEN IF `the corporation is a distributing corporation`
                 THEN `may examine the records during the usual business hours and take extracts, on payment of a reasonable fee`
                 ELSE `has no right of access under s 21(1)`
        OTHERWISE `may examine the records during the usual business hours and take extracts, free of charge`

-- src:276 | (2) A shareholder of a corporation is entitled on request and without charge to one copy of the articles and by-laws and of any unanimous shareholder agreement.
@ref CBCA s 21(2) copies of corporate records (src:276)
GIVEN `the person is a shareholder of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has requested a copy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the shareholder is entitled to one copy of the articles, by-laws and any unanimous shareholder agreement, without charge, within s 21(2)` MEANS
        `the person is a shareholder of the corporation`
    AND `the person has requested a copy`

-- s 21(3): shareholders and creditors, their personal representatives, the Director and, if the corporation
-- is distributing, any other person, "on payment of a reasonable fee and on sending ... the affidavit
-- referred to in subsection (7)", may require a basic list: provided within 10 days after receipt of the
-- affidavit and "made up to a date not more than 10 days before the date of receipt".
-- src:278 | (3) Shareholders and creditors of a corporation, their personal representatives, the Director and, if the corporation is a distributing corporation, any other person, on payment of a reasonable fee and on sending to a corporation or its agent or mandatary the affidavit referred to in subsection (7), may on application require the corporation or its agent or mandatary to provide within 10 days after the receipt of the affidavit a list (in this section referred to as the “basic list”) made up to a date not more than 10 days before the date of receipt of the affidavit setting out the names of the shareholders of the corporation, the number of shares owned by each shareholder and the address of each shareholder as shown on the records of the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 21(3) shareholder lists (src:278)
GIVEN person IS A `Person seeking to examine the corporate records (s 21)`
      `the corporation is a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: section 2(1) (keel)
      `the person has paid a reasonable fee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has sent the corporation or its agent or mandatary the affidavit referred to in subsection 21(7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person may require the corporation to provide a basic list within s 21(3)` MEANS
        (person EQUALS `any other person` IMPLIES `the corporation is a distributing corporation`)
    AND `the person has paid a reasonable fee`
    AND `the person has sent the corporation or its agent or mandatary the affidavit referred to in subsection 21(7)`

-- src:278 | (3) Shareholders and creditors of a corporation, their personal representatives, the Director and, if the corporation is a distributing corporation, any other person, on payment of a reasonable fee and on sending to a corporation or its agent or mandatary the affidavit referred to in subsection (7), may on application require the corporation or its agent or mandatary to provide within 10 days after the receipt of the affidavit a list (in this section referred to as the “basic list”) made up to a date not more than 10 days before the date of receipt of the affidavit setting out the names of the shareholders of the corporation, the number of shares owned by each shareholder and the address of each shareholder as shown on the records of the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 21(3) shareholder lists (src:278)
DECIDE `the ten-day limit of s 21(3)` IS `Time limit` WITH
    `number of units` IS 10
    `unit of time` IS `calendar days`

-- src:278 | (3) Shareholders and creditors of a corporation, their personal representatives, the Director and, if the corporation is a distributing corporation, any other person, on payment of a reasonable fee and on sending to a corporation or its agent or mandatary the affidavit referred to in subsection (7), may on application require the corporation or its agent or mandatary to provide within 10 days after the receipt of the affidavit a list (in this section referred to as the “basic list”) made up to a date not more than 10 days before the date of receipt of the affidavit setting out the names of the shareholders of the corporation, the number of shares owned by each shareholder and the address of each shareholder as shown on the records of the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 21(3) shareholder lists (src:278)
GIVEN `the day the corporation received the affidavit` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to provide the basic list within s 21(3)` MEANS
    `the last day of` `the ten-day limit of s 21(3)` `counted from` `the day the corporation received the affidavit`

-- src:278 | (3) Shareholders and creditors of a corporation, their personal representatives, the Director and, if the corporation is a distributing corporation, any other person, on payment of a reasonable fee and on sending to a corporation or its agent or mandatary the affidavit referred to in subsection (7), may on application require the corporation or its agent or mandatary to provide within 10 days after the receipt of the affidavit a list (in this section referred to as the “basic list”) made up to a date not more than 10 days before the date of receipt of the affidavit setting out the names of the shareholders of the corporation, the number of shares owned by each shareholder and the address of each shareholder as shown on the records of the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 21(3) shareholder lists (src:278)
GIVEN `the day the corporation received the affidavit` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the earliest date the basic list may be made up to within s 21(3)` MEANS
    `the earliest day allowed by` `the ten-day limit of s 21(3)` `counted back from` `the day the corporation received the affidavit`

-- src:278 | (3) Shareholders and creditors of a corporation, their personal representatives, the Director and, if the corporation is a distributing corporation, any other person, on payment of a reasonable fee and on sending to a corporation or its agent or mandatary the affidavit referred to in subsection (7), may on application require the corporation or its agent or mandatary to provide within 10 days after the receipt of the affidavit a list (in this section referred to as the “basic list”) made up to a date not more than 10 days before the date of receipt of the affidavit setting out the names of the shareholders of the corporation, the number of shares owned by each shareholder and the address of each shareholder as shown on the records of the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 21(3) shareholder lists (src:278)
GIVEN `the day the corporation received the affidavit` IS A DATE
      `the day the basic list was provided` IS A DATE
      `the date the basic list is made up to` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation has provided the basic list as s 21(3) requires` MEANS
        `done within the time limit` `the ten-day limit of s 21(3)` `the day the corporation received the affidavit` `the day the basic list was provided`
    AND `the date the basic list is made up to` AT LEAST (`the earliest date the basic list may be made up to within s 21(3)` `the day the corporation received the affidavit`)
    AND `the date the basic list is made up to` AT MOST `the day the corporation received the affidavit`

-- src:280 | (4) A person requiring a corporation to provide a basic list may, by stating in the affidavit referred to in subsection (3) that they require supplemental lists, require the corporation or its agent or mandatary on payment of a reasonable fee to provide supplemental lists setting out any changes from the basic list in the names or addresses of the shareholders and the number of shares owned by each shareholder for each business day following the date the basic list is made up to.
@ref CBCA s 21(4) supplemental lists (src:280)
GIVEN `the person required a basic list under subsection 21(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit states that the person requires supplemental lists` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has paid a reasonable fee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person may require supplemental lists within s 21(4)` MEANS
        `the person required a basic list under subsection 21(3)`
    AND `the affidavit states that the person requires supplemental lists`
    AND `the person has paid a reasonable fee`

-- s 21(5): a supplemental list is due (a) on the date the basic list is furnished, where its information
-- relates to changes before that date, and (b) on the business day following the day to which the list
-- relates, where it relates to changes on or after that date. "Business day" is not defined in the text,
-- and no calendar of holidays is among the sources, so the business day that follows is an input.
-- src:282 | (5) The corporation or its agent or mandatary shall provide a supplemental list required under subsection (4)
-- src:283 | (a) on the date the basic list is furnished, where the information relates to changes that took place prior to that date; and
-- src:284 | (b) on the business day following the day to which the supplemental list relates, where the information relates to changes that take place on or after the date the basic list is furnished.
@ref CBCA s 21(5) when supplemental lists to be provided (src:282-284)
GIVEN `the date the basic list is furnished` IS A DATE
      `the day to which the supplemental list relates` IS A DATE
      `the business day following the day to which the supplemental list relates` IS A DATE   -- out of range: "business day" is not defined in the text (not in the sources)
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the supplemental list is due within s 21(5)` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the day to which the supplemental list relates` AT LEAST `the date the basic list is furnished`)
    THEN `the date the basic list is furnished`
    ELSE `the business day following the day to which the supplemental list relates`

-- src:286 | (6) A person requiring a corporation to furnish a basic list or a supplemental list may also require the corporation to include in that list the name and address of any known holder of an option or right to acquire shares of the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 21(6) holders of options (src:286)
GIVEN `the person requires a basic list or a supplemental list` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person may also require the list to include the known holders of options within s 21(6)` MEANS
    `the person requires a basic list or a supplemental list`

-- s 21(7) and s 21(8): what the affidavit says, and who swears it where the applicant is a body corporate.
-- src:288 | (7) The affidavit required under subsection (1.1) or (3) shall state
-- src:289 | (a) the name and address of the applicant;
-- src:290 | (b) the name and address for service of the body corporate, if the applicant is a body corporate; and
-- src:291 | (c) that the basic list and any supplemental lists obtained pursuant to subsection (4) or the information contained in the securities register obtained pursuant to subsection (1.1), as the case may be, will not be used except as permitted under subsection (9).
@ref CBCA s 21(7) contents of affidavit (src:288-291)
DECLARE `Affidavit under s 21(7)` HAS
    `states the name and address of the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the applicant is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `states the name and address for service of the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `states that the lists or the securities register information will not be used except as permitted under subsection 21(9)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is made by a director or officer of the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:288 | (7) The affidavit required under subsection (1.1) or (3) shall state
-- src:289 | (a) the name and address of the applicant;
-- src:290 | (b) the name and address for service of the body corporate, if the applicant is a body corporate; and
-- src:291 | (c) that the basic list and any supplemental lists obtained pursuant to subsection (4) or the information contained in the securities register obtained pursuant to subsection (1.1), as the case may be, will not be used except as permitted under subsection (9).
-- src:293 | (8) If the applicant is a body corporate, the affidavit shall be made by a director or officer of the body corporate.
@ref CBCA s 21(7), s 21(8) contents of affidavit (src:288-291 src:293)
GIVEN affidavit IS AN `Affidavit under s 21(7)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the affidavit has the contents s 21(7) and s 21(8) require` MEANS
        affidavit's `states the name and address of the applicant`
    AND (affidavit's `the applicant is a body corporate` IMPLIES affidavit's `states the name and address for service of the body corporate`)
    AND affidavit's `states that the lists or the securities register information will not be used except as permitted under subsection 21(9)`
    AND (affidavit's `the applicant is a body corporate` IMPLIES affidavit's `is made by a director or officer of the body corporate`)

-- s 21(9): the use of a list or of securities register information.
-- src:295 | (9) A list of shareholders or information from a securities register obtained under this section shall not be used by any person except in connection with
-- src:296 | (a) an effort to influence the voting of shareholders of the corporation;
-- src:297 | (b) an offer to acquire securities of the corporation; or
-- src:298 | (c) any other matter relating to the affairs of the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 21(9) use of information or shareholder list (src:295-298)
DECLARE `Use of a shareholder list or securities register information (s 21(9))` IS ONE OF
    `an effort to influence the voting of shareholders of the corporation`
    `an offer to acquire securities of the corporation`
    `any other matter relating to the affairs of the corporation`
    `any other use`

-- src:295 | (9) A list of shareholders or information from a securities register obtained under this section shall not be used by any person except in connection with
-- src:296 | (a) an effort to influence the voting of shareholders of the corporation;
-- src:297 | (b) an offer to acquire securities of the corporation; or
-- src:298 | (c) any other matter relating to the affairs of the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 21(9) use of information or shareholder list (src:295-298)
GIVEN use IS A `Use of a shareholder list or securities register information (s 21(9))`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the use of the list or information is permitted within s 21(9)` MEANS
    CONSIDER use
    WHEN `an effort to influence the voting of shareholders of the corporation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an offer to acquire securities of the corporation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `any other matter relating to the affairs of the corporation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `any other use` THEN FALSE

-- src:300 | (10) A person who, without reasonable cause, contravenes this section is guilty of an offence and liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to both.
@ref CBCA s 21(10) offence (src:300)
GIVEN `the person contravenes section 21` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is guilty of an offence within s 21(10)` MEANS
        `the person contravenes section 21`
    AND (NOT `the person has reasonable cause`)

-- "a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to both"
-- src:300 | (10) A person who, without reasonable cause, contravenes this section is guilty of an offence and liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to both.
@ref CBCA s 21(10) offence (src:300)
GIVETH A `Maximum punishment for an offence in Parts I to VI`
`the most a court may impose on summary conviction within s 21(10)` MEANS
    `Maximum punishment for an offence in Parts I to VI` WITH
        `maximum fine in dollars` IS 5000
        `maximum imprisonment in months` IS JUST 6

§§ `s 22 form of records; precautions`

-- src:419 | 22 (1) All registers and other records required by this Act to be prepared and maintained may be in a bound or loose-leaf form or in a photographic film form, or may be entered or recorded by any system of mechanical or electronic data processing or any other information storage device that is capable of reproducing any required information in intelligible written form within a reasonable time.
@ref CBCA s 22(1) form of records (src:419)
DECLARE `Form of a register or other record (s 22(1))` IS ONE OF
    `a bound form`
    `a loose-leaf form`
    `a photographic film form`
    `entered or recorded by a system of mechanical or electronic data processing or any other information storage device`
    `any other form`

-- src:419 | 22 (1) All registers and other records required by this Act to be prepared and maintained may be in a bound or loose-leaf form or in a photographic film form, or may be entered or recorded by any system of mechanical or electronic data processing or any other information storage device that is capable of reproducing any required information in intelligible written form within a reasonable time.
@ref CBCA s 22(1) form of records (src:419)
GIVEN form IS A `Form of a register or other record (s 22(1))`
      `the system or device is capable of reproducing any required information in intelligible written form within a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the form of the record is permitted within s 22(1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER form
    WHEN `a bound form` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a loose-leaf form` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a photographic film form` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `entered or recorded by a system of mechanical or electronic data processing or any other information storage device` THEN `the system or device is capable of reproducing any required information in intelligible written form within a reasonable time`
    WHEN `any other form` THEN FALSE

-- src:421 | (2) A corporation or its agents or mandataries shall take reasonable precautions to
-- src:422 | (a) prevent loss or destruction of,
-- src:423 | (b) prevent falsification of entries in, and
-- src:424 | (c) facilitate detection and correction of inaccuracies in
-- src:425 | the registers and other records required by this Act to be prepared and maintained.
@ref CBCA s 22(2) precautions (src:421-425)
GIVEN `the corporation or its agents or mandataries have taken reasonable precautions to prevent loss or destruction of the registers and other records` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation or its agents or mandataries have taken reasonable precautions to prevent falsification of entries in the registers and other records` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation or its agents or mandataries have taken reasonable precautions to facilitate detection and correction of inaccuracies in the registers and other records` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation or its agents or mandataries have taken the precautions s 22(2) requires` MEANS
        `the corporation or its agents or mandataries have taken reasonable precautions to prevent loss or destruction of the registers and other records`
    AND `the corporation or its agents or mandataries have taken reasonable precautions to prevent falsification of entries in the registers and other records`
    AND `the corporation or its agents or mandataries have taken reasonable precautions to facilitate detection and correction of inaccuracies in the registers and other records`

-- src:427 | (3) A person who, without reasonable cause, contravenes this section is guilty of an offence and liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to both.
@ref CBCA s 22(3) offence (src:427)
GIVEN `the person contravenes section 22` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is guilty of an offence within s 22(3)` MEANS
        `the person contravenes section 22`
    AND (NOT `the person has reasonable cause`)

-- src:427 | (3) A person who, without reasonable cause, contravenes this section is guilty of an offence and liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to both.
@ref CBCA s 22(3) offence (src:427)
GIVETH A `Maximum punishment for an offence in Parts I to VI`
`the most a court may impose on summary conviction within s 22(3)` MEANS
    `Maximum punishment for an offence in Parts I to VI` WITH
        `maximum fine in dollars` IS 5000
        `maximum imprisonment in months` IS JUST 6

§§ `s 23 corporate seal`

-- src:429 | 23 (1) A corporation may, but need not, adopt a corporate seal, and may change a corporate seal that is adopted.
@ref CBCA s 23(1) corporate seal (src:429)
GIVEN `the body is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may adopt, and may change, a corporate seal within s 23(1)` MEANS
    `the body is a corporation`

-- src:429 | 23 (1) A corporation may, but need not, adopt a corporate seal, and may change a corporate seal that is adopted.
@ref CBCA s 23(1) corporate seal (src:429)
GIVEN `the body is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation must adopt a corporate seal within s 23(1)` MEANS
    FALSE

-- src:431 | (2) A document executed or, in Quebec, signed on behalf of a corporation is not invalid merely because a corporate seal is not affixed to it.
@ref CBCA s 23(2) validity of unsealed documents (src:431)
GIVEN `the document was executed or, in Quebec, signed on behalf of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a corporate seal is not affixed to it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is invalid on a ground other than that a corporate seal is not affixed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the document is invalid within s 23(2)` MEANS
    `the document is invalid on a ground other than that a corporate seal is not affixed`
